## The recurring defects on this track and the cookbook chapter that fixes each
Do not re-explain the problem back — apply the recipe (the named chapters are printed in full
under **Recipes** at the end of this brief) and change the numbers.  If the judge repeated an issue from the previous round, the earlier fix was too
timid: double the amplitude / the count / the contrast this time.

| what the judge wrote | fix it with |
|---|---|
| flat / one-colour ground, no paths, hard raised-bed edges | `"Ground that reads real"` — vertex-colour blend, carve the path into `heightAt`, dress the seams |
| a hard world edge against the sky, missing horizon | `"Horizon: the world must not end"` — ground ≥ 2.4 × fog far, fog = sky horizon colour, silhouette ring at 0.6 × fog far |
| the backdrop looks like flat / beige / untextured cut-outs | same chapter, rules 4-5 — solid geometry, darken the base colour, never lerp it toward the fog colour |
| a pond / terrace is a hard-edged plane sitting on the ground | carve it into `heightAt` in `src/env.js` and dress the seam (`"Ground that reads real"`) |
| "camera is N m below ground level" | the terrain lifted the floor: flatten `heightAt` toward y = 0 inside the bounds, or add `heightAt(x, z)` to that camera's y in `src/scene.js` |
| identical cones / stacked blocks / primitive repetition | `"Vegetation that reads real"`, `"Rocks, cliffs and boulders that read organic"` — 3+ silhouettes, clustered, scale/hue jitter, no axis-aligned stacks |
| sparse, token, "a diorama on a plane", empty midground | `"Set dressing"` + `"Scene layering"` — hit the per-zone prop counts, add a foreground element 2-4 m from each camera |
| flat / dark / monochrome light, black shade, jagged shadows | `"Atmosphere: time-of-day triads with numbers"` — warm key vs cool fill ≥ 60° apart, shadow texel ≤ 0.05 m |
| frames at t=0 and t=1.5 identical, "nothing moves" | `"Motion you can SEE between t = 0 and t = 1.5 s"` — the hook is `userData.update` (never `tick`), amplitudes from the table |
| camera inside geometry / shows only sky or a wall | move the camera in `src/scene.js` and mask scatter within 6 m of it (`cameraMask`) |
